    "problem": "Forecasting future climate responses to massive carbon emissions is challenging because modern observations provide limited insight into carbon-cycle dynamics and climate sensitivity, particularly the role of feedbacks, under the extremely high CO2 concentrations projected for the future.",
    "method": "The paper proposes using past greenhouse warming episodes from the early Cenozoic as natural experiments to understand climate and carbon-cycle coupling, which can help predict the consequences of future unabated carbon emissions.",
    "task": "The task is to use past episodes of greenhouse warming from the early Cenozoic to understand the coupling of climate and the carbon cycle, thereby helping to predict the consequences of future unabated carbon emissions.",
